Candid editorial photograph. Photojournalism aesthetic. Feels trustworthy
and grounded — not alarming, not exploitative, not a stock photo cliché.

CRITICAL: absolutely NO text, letters, numbers, words, captions, headlines,
signs, billboards, logos, or any written characters anywhere in the image.
The image must be purely visual. Any text added by the model will be cropped
out downstream, so prioritize the subject and composition.

Subject context (informs mood and setting, NOT a literal directive):
- Product / situation: {{ case.product or case.harm_type or "consumer situation" }}
- Audience: {{ icp.demographics }}

Editorial angle for this variant: "{{ angle }}"
{% if angle == "informative" -%}
Mood: neutral daylight, subject calmly reviewing documents or looking
thoughtfully to the side. Desk, home office, or cafe setting. Cool, muted
color palette. Documentary feel.
{%- elif angle == "empathetic" -%}
Mood: warm natural light, subject in a moment of quiet reflection. Hands
visible, relaxed posture. Warm color palette — amber, soft gold, cream.
Human dignity first; no distress, no staging.
{%- elif angle == "urgent" -%}
Mood: slightly crisper composition, subject mid-action (checking a phone,
opening mail, on a call). Cooler palette. Subtle time cues allowed — a
window with afternoon light, a partially visible calendar — but NO clocks
with readable numbers and NO text on any surface.
{%- else -%}
Mood: balanced, editorial.
{%- endif %}

Composition:
- Single human subject, shoulders-up or medium shot, 1:1 square framing for
  Meta feed placement.
- Natural skin tones and clothing; no branded apparel.
- Avoid: gavels, scales of justice, judges, police, courtroom imagery,
  stock-photo legal iconography, anything implying an official legal notice.

Tone notes from ICP targeting hints: {{ icp.targeting_hints }}
